{
 "doc": "PROFILE.md §6.2: 'The four report the bits the packed classification-flags byte carried, in the order Synthetic, KeyPoint, Withheld, Overlap' -- the mapping itself, which the three other cases in this group do not reach because every shipped fixture has all four flag bits clear. The case builds its own non-zero input instead of shipping one: four pipelines each set exactly one flag with `filters.assign`, and each output is read back with an independent LAS reader that decodes the packed byte bit by bit. All four bits are pinned non-zero in turn -- Synthetic at bit 0, KeyPoint at bit 1, Withheld at bit 2, Overlap at bit 3 -- so transposing any pair of them fails this case. The read-back is deliberately not `pdal info`: an implementation that swapped two bits consistently on both its write and read paths would agree with itself, and only a reader outside the candidate's own code can tell the difference.",
